WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.083
(bouncy piano music)

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:15.123
- [Narrator] Kenenisa
Bekele is one of the world's

00:00:15.123 --> 00:00:16.990
fastest marathon runners.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:20.332
He runs the 26.2 miles in half the time

00:00:20.332 --> 00:00:22.665
it takes the average runner.

00:00:36.015 --> 00:00:37.313
- [Narrator] He has
explored the boundaries

00:00:37.313 --> 00:00:40.142
of human potential and
pushed his body to places

00:00:40.142 --> 00:00:42.975
that only few could ever dream of.

00:00:49.874 --> 00:00:52.009
Every year, the world's
top marathon runners

00:00:52.009 --> 00:00:54.352
come to the Berlin Marathon
with hopes of breaking

00:00:54.352 --> 00:00:56.483
the world record, running a marathon

00:00:56.483 --> 00:01:00.514
under two hours, two
minutes, and 57 seconds,

00:01:00.514 --> 00:01:03.597
and in 2016, Kenenisa almost beat it.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:23.187
- [Narrator] While other cities
host marathons each year,

00:01:23.187 --> 00:01:25.314
the world's leading runners
have their sights set

00:01:25.314 --> 00:01:27.397
on this particular track.

00:01:48.239 --> 00:01:50.338
- [Narrator] The human body
is not built to run marathons

00:01:50.338 --> 00:01:54.332
at Kenenisa's desired speed,
so for the last 15 years,

00:01:54.332 --> 00:01:56.780
Kenenisa has been
putting in the hard work,

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:59.995
training twice a day, every day.

00:01:59.995 --> 00:02:02.167
But pushing his body to unthinkable limits

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:06.250
means the possibilities
of getting hurt are high.

00:02:33.578 --> 00:02:36.838
- [Narrator] And Kenenisa
shows no signs of slowing down.

00:02:36.838 --> 00:02:39.158
He continues to explore his body's limits

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:41.569
in the hopes of achieving
his ultimate goal.

00:02:41.569 --> 00:02:45.736
(lively, bouncy music)
(audience cheering)

00:03:12.134 --> 00:03:14.717
(bell chiming)

